goals:
• Configure OSPF within AS {{confederation_as}} so the routers know how to reach each others loopback interfaces.
  AS {{confederation_as}}: {{router1_name}}, {{router2_name}}, {{router5_name}}, {{router6_name}}
• Configure IBGP within AS {{confederation_as}} but create confederations, use AS {{router6_member_as}}, AS {{router2_member_as}}, AS {{router5_member_as}} and AS {{router1_member_as}}.
  AS {{router6_member_as}}: {{router6_name}}
  AS {{router2_member_as}}: {{router2_name}}
  AS {{router5_member_as}}: {{router5_name}}
  AS {{router1_member_as}}: {{router1_name}}
• Configure EBGP between AS {{external_as1}} and AS {{confederation_as}}.
  AS {{external_as1}}: {{router3_name}}
  AS {{confederation_as}}: {{router2_name}}, {{router6_name}}
• Configure EBGP between AS {{external_as2}} and AS {{confederation_as}}.
  AS {{external_as2}}: {{router4_name}}
  AS {{confederation_as}}: {{router1_name}}, {{router5_name}}
• Advertise all loopback0 interfaces in BGP.
• Ensure all loopback0 interfaces are reachable throughout the BGP network.
